{
  "slug": "one-character-any-scene",
  "name": "One Character, Any Scene — Without Masks or Training",
  "description": "Two source images — one generated, one uploaded — and five one-line prompts that mix them: face from one, body from the other; swap the order; keep the stage, change the star; move her off the runway into the studio; borrow the jacket and the setting. No masks, no inpainting, no LoRA — just {image:1:person}, {image:2:face}, {image:2:settings} in the prompt.",
  "markdownDescription": "# One Character, Any Scene — Without Masks or Training\n\nFive results from **two source images** and five short prompts. Nothing else: no masks, no inpainting, no LoRA, no character training.\n\n## The two sources\n1. **The star** — a generated image (GPT Image 2, 2K, 16:9): a supermodel on the runway.\n2. **The reference** — an uploaded photo: her face, her jacket, her studio.\n\nBoth feed the **References** input of every result node. In the prompt you address them by position — `{image:1}` is the first reference, `{image:2}` the second — and you name the *part* you want with a role word after the colon: `person`, `face`, `background`, `settings`, `jacket`.\n\n## The five combinations\n| Result | Prompt | What it shows |\n|---|---|---|\n| Face from one. Body from the other. | `{image:1:person} with {image:2:face}` | Compose one identity from two people |\n| Swap the order. Swap the result. | `{image:2:person} with {image:1:face}` | Position is meaning — reverse it and the roles flip |\n| Keep the stage. Change the star. | `{image:1:background} with {image:2:person}` | Take only the setting from a reference |\n| Off the runway, into the studio | `{image:1:person} in {image:2:settings}` | Move a character into another scene |\n| Her jacket. Her studio. Your model. | `{image:1:person} wearing {image:2:jacket} at {image:2:settings}` | Borrow one garment + the place, keep the person |\n\n## Make it yours\nSwap the uploaded reference for your own photo (or the star for your own character), keep the prompts, run all five. Works with GPT Image 2 and Nano Banana Pro — both are used here.\n\n## Tips\n- Say what you want to take from each reference — a role word (`face`, `jacket`, `background`) beats a long description.\n- Order matters: `{image:1}` / `{image:2}` follow the order the references were connected — check the References list on the node before rewriting a prompt.\n- One thing per role; the model resolves the rest.\n",
